.TH QCCTLD 8 "2026-10-25" "qcctl" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qcctld \- qcctl daemon: profile drift watch, fan strategy, status publisher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcctld
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qcctld
is
.BR always " resident,"
whether or not a fan strategy is configured. Applying a profile is something it does at
startup, not its reason to exist. It runs under systemd as
.IR qcctld.service ,
which passes
.BR \-\-foreground .
.PP
It owns the
.B single
.BR qcstats (1)
instance: two samplers would mean two observer effects on the quantity being reported.
Everything it decides comes from that one stream, read as NDJSON over a pipe.
.PP
What it does, continuously:
.TP
\(bu
.B Watches the applied profile for drift,
re\-checking every
.B \-\-drift\-interval
milliseconds that each applied setting still reads back as it was asked for. Something
else on the system moving a clock is reported rather than silently corrected.
.TP
\(bu
.B Runs the fan strategy
from
.IR /etc/qcctl/fan.config ,
if the profile in force hands the fan over. Ownership is taken through the thermal
zone's
.I mode
attribute \- never by writing PWM \- so the kernel's own protections stay underneath at
all times. The ceiling at 85 degrees is not configurable.
.TP
\(bu
.B Publishes a status snapshot
to
.B \-\-status\-file
for anything that wants to display state, and the active profile name to
.BR \-\-active\-file .
.TP
\(bu
.B Serves the control socket,
mode 0666 so that any local user can reach it. Its vocabulary is the restriction: a
client can ask to
.I raise
cooling and nothing else. It cannot lower cooling, release the zone, or change a
profile. See
.B \-\-cool\-max
in
.BR qcctl (8).
.TP
\(bu
.B Judges airflow
against
.IR /var/lib/qcctl/fan-baseline ,
when one has been captured and
.IR fan.config 's
.B < AIRFLOW >
block names a delta.
.PP
If the sampler dies the fan is released
.B first
and the sampler then retried: a strategy cannot be driven without temperatures, and
holding the zone while blind is the one thing it must never do. If the retries are
exhausted it exits non\-zero so that systemd restarts the unit \- in\-process retries
handle a hiccup, systemd handles a persistent fault.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path" "\fR, \fP" \-\-config " path"
Profiles. Default
.IR /etc/qcctl/profiles.conf .
.TP
.BI \-\-fan\-config " path"
Fan strategy. Default
.IR /etc/qcctl/fan.config .
.TP
.BI \-\-state " path"
Boot\-state snapshot. Default
.IR /var/lib/qcctl/boot-state .
.TP
.BI \-\-pidfile " path"
Default
.IR /run/qcctl/pid .
.TP
.BI \-\-status\-file " path"
Where the status snapshot is published. Default
.IR /run/qcctl/status .
.TP
.BI \-\-control\-socket " path"
Where unprivileged clients ask for cooling. Default
.IR /run/qcctl/control .
.TP
.BI \-\-fan\-baseline\-file " path"
The captured rpm\-per\-state reference. Default
.IR /var/lib/qcctl/fan-baseline .
.TP
.BI \-\-active\-file " path"
Where the active profile name is recorded, for the resume hook to read. Default
.IR /run/qcctl/active .
.TP
.BI \-\-selection\-file " path"
The operator's recorded choice, honoured on a restart. Scoped to the boot id: a power
cycle returns to the DEFAULT profile. Default
.IR /var/lib/qcctl/selected .
.TP
.BI \-\-drift\-interval " ms"
How often to re\-check that the applied profile still holds. Default 10000.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIname\fR|\fIid\fR
Profile to apply at startup. Default: the profile marked DEFAULT.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-apply
Run the fan strategy only; do not apply a profile.
.TP
.B \-\-oneshot
Apply, then exit without running a strategy. Implies
.BR \-\-foreground .
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Stay in the foreground and log to stdout, which is what the unit passes. The default is
to detach once the pidfile is held, and log to syslog.
.TP
.BI \-\-stats\-cmd " cmd"
Override the sampler command. Exists for the tests, which feed a canned NDJSON stream
instead of running
.BR qcstats (1).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT ", " SIGHUP
Stop at the next loop iteration, releasing the fan and handing the zone back to the
kernel on the way out. The state it leaves is either 0 or the cooling map's own floor,
which is what the governor would hold there.
.TP
.B SIGPIPE
Ignored: the sampler dying must not kill the daemon.
.PP
.I qcctld.service
also carries
.B ExecStopPost=qcctl-fan-release
as a backstop, for the stop this process did not get to handle itself \-
.BR SIGKILL ,
or a crash.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/qcctld.service
The unit.
.B Restart=on-failure
with
.BR RestartSec=5 .
.TP
.I /etc/qcctl/profiles.conf
.TQ
.I /etc/qcctl/fan.config
Configuration; see
.BR qcctl (8).
.TP
.I /var/lib/qcctl/boot-state
.TQ
.I /var/lib/qcctl/selected
.TQ
.I /var/lib/qcctl/fan-baseline
State that survives a restart.
.TP
.I /run/qcctl/
.IR pid ", " active ", " status " and " control ,
all created at startup.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QCCTL_SYSROOT
Read and write under this directory instead of
.IR / .
.B Not for production use;
see
.BR qcctl (8).
.TP
.B QCCTL_SAMPLER_RETRY_MS
.TQ
.B QCCTL_FANWD_INTERVAL_MS
.TQ
.B QCCTL_FANWD_FORGET_MS
Shorten the sampler retry delay, the fan watchdog's interval, and its forget window.
These exist so the tests can reach behaviour that otherwise takes minutes of wall clock,
and are documented here because a reader of the journal may see their effect.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Asked to stop, and stopped.
.TP
.B non-zero
A fault systemd should act on \- the configuration did not parse or apply, the pidfile
could not be held, or the sampler could not be recovered.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qcctl (8),
.BR qcstats (1)
.PP
.I /usr/share/doc/qcctl/USAGE.md
documents the configuration formats and how to read the status output.
.SH AUTHOR
Hans Kramer.
